<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rspec xmlns="http://www.geni.net/resources/rspec/3"
       xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.geni.net/resources/rspec/3 http://www.geni.net/resources/rspec/3/request.xsd"
       type="request">
  <rspec_tour xmlns="http://www.protogeni.net/resources/rspec/ext/apt-tour/1">
    <description type="markdown">QBR compact three-node bare-metal profile: one combined client/dispatcher and two execution hosts at CloudLab Utah.</description>
    <instructions type="markdown">Roles and experiment IP addresses:
- client: 10.10.1.1 - load generator, ingress dispatcher, and post-run log collection.
- worker1: 10.10.1.11 - RPC execution, shared queue, and migration controller.
- worker2: 10.10.1.12 - RPC execution, shared queue, and migration controller.

Run the load generator and dispatcher on different physical cores on client.
Measure their local handoff cost and CPU/NIC utilization; keep the arrangement
identical for every scheduling method. Do not treat this as an isolated dispatcher.
Start each worker with eight execution cores and one separate controller core.
Select CPU IDs after inspecting NUMA/SMT topology; the profile does not pin CPUs.

Use experiment IPs for requests, replies, feedback, and migration.
Collect logs after timed runs. Each LAN attachment requests 25 Gbps.
This topology supports two-host migration and basic scheduling comparisons.
It does not validate two independent sources migrating to a third destination.
Same-site placement does not guarantee the same physical rack.
Resources only: no scheduler software is installed or started.
</instructions>
  </rspec_tour>
  <node client_id="client" exclusive="true" component_manager_id="urn:publicid:IDN+utah.cloudlab.us+authority+cm">
    <sliver_type name="raw">
      <disk_image name="urn:publicid:IDN+emulab.net+image+emulab-ops//UBUNTU22-64-STD"/>
    </sliver_type>
    <hardware_type name="c6525-25g"/>
    <interface client_id="client:if0">
      <ip address="10.10.1.1" netmask="255.255.255.0" type="ipv4"/>
    </interface>
  </node>
  <node client_id="worker1" exclusive="true" component_manager_id="urn:publicid:IDN+utah.cloudlab.us+authority+cm">
    <sliver_type name="raw">
      <disk_image name="urn:publicid:IDN+emulab.net+image+emulab-ops//UBUNTU22-64-STD"/>
    </sliver_type>
    <hardware_type name="c6525-25g"/>
    <interface client_id="worker1:if0">
      <ip address="10.10.1.11" netmask="255.255.255.0" type="ipv4"/>
    </interface>
  </node>
  <node client_id="worker2" exclusive="true" component_manager_id="urn:publicid:IDN+utah.cloudlab.us+authority+cm">
    <sliver_type name="raw">
      <disk_image name="urn:publicid:IDN+emulab.net+image+emulab-ops//UBUNTU22-64-STD"/>
    </sliver_type>
    <hardware_type name="c6525-25g"/>
    <interface client_id="worker2:if0">
      <ip address="10.10.1.12" netmask="255.255.255.0" type="ipv4"/>
    </interface>
  </node>
  <link client_id="exp-lan">
    <interface_ref client_id="client:if0"/>
    <interface_ref client_id="worker1:if0"/>
    <interface_ref client_id="worker2:if0"/>
    <link_type name="lan"/>
    <component_manager name="urn:publicid:IDN+utah.cloudlab.us+authority+cm"/>
    <property source_id="client:if0" dest_id="exp-lan" capacity="25000000"/>
    <property source_id="worker1:if0" dest_id="exp-lan" capacity="25000000"/>
    <property source_id="worker2:if0" dest_id="exp-lan" capacity="25000000"/>
  </link>
</rspec>
